
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main()
{
    char names[500][30], temp[30], key[30];
    int n, i, j, found = 0;

    printf("Enter number of residents: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);

    // Read resident names
    printf("Enter resident names:\n");

    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        scanf(" %29[^\n]", names[i]);
    }

    // Sort names alphabetically using Bubble Sort
    for(i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)
    {
        for(j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++)
        {
            if(strcmp(names[j], names[j + 1]) > 0)
            {
                strcpy(temp, names[j]);
                strcpy(names[j], names[j + 1]);
                strcpy(names[j + 1], temp);
            }
        }
    }

    // Display sorted names
    printf("\nNames in alphabetical order:\n");

    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        printf("%s\n", names[i]);
    }

    // Search resident
    printf("\nEnter name to search: ");
    scanf(" %29[^\n]", key);

    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if(strcmp(names[i], key) == 0)
        {
            printf("Resident found at position %d\n", i + 1);
            found = 1;
            break;
        }
    }

    if(!found)
        printf("Resident not found\n");

    // Find duplicate entries
    printf("\nDuplicate names:\n");

    found = 0;

    for(i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)
    {
        if(strcmp(names[i], names[i + 1]) == 0)
        {
            printf("%s\n", names[i]);
            found = 1;

            // Skip repeated copies of the same name
            while(i < n - 1 &&
                  strcmp(names[i], names[i + 1]) == 0)
            {
                i++;
            }
        }
    }

    if(!found)
        printf("No duplicate names found\n");

    return 0;
}
Pseudocode
1. Start.
2. Read the number of residents n.
3. Read all resident names into a 2D character array.
4. Sort names alphabetically using Bubble Sort:
   - Compare adjacent names using strcmp().
   - If the first name comes after the second, swap them using strcpy().
5. Display the sorted names.
6. Read the name to search.
7. Compare the search name with each resident name using strcmp().
8. If matched, display the position; otherwise display "Resident not found".
9. Check adjacent sorted names for duplicates.
10. Display duplicate names.
11. Stop.

